ct/obs-studio/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/obsproject/obs-studio/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/obsproject/obs-studio/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/obsproject/obs-studio/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/obsproject/obs-studio/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/obsproject/obs-studio/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/obsproject/obs-studio/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/obsproject/obs-studio/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/obsproject/obs-studio/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/obsproject/obs-studio/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/obsproject/obs-studio/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/obsproject/obs-studio/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/obsproject/obs-studio/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/obsproject/obs-studio/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/obsproject/obs-studio/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/obsproject/obs-studio/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/obsproject/obs-studio/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/obsproject/obs-studio/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/obsproject/obs-studio/deployments","created_at":"2013-10-01T02:40:31Z","updated_at":"2025-12-13T01:03:06Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-13T00:44:28Z","git_url":"git://github.com/obsproject/obs-studio.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:obsproject/obs-studio.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/obsproject/obs-studio.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/obsproject/obs-studio","homepage":"https://obsproject.com","size":78691,"stargazers_count":68667,"watchers_count":68667,"language":"C","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":8873,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":1052,"license":{"key":"gpl-2.0","name":"GNU General Public License v2.0","spdx_id":"GPL-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/gpl-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTg="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["c","c-plus-plus","directshow","facebook-live","ffmpeg","game-capture","live-streaming","screen-capture","twitch-tv","video-recording","youtube-live"],"visibility":"public","forks":8873,"open_issues":1052,"watchers":68667,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/obsproject/obs-studio/pulls/6134","html_url":"https://github.com/obsproject/obs-studio/pull/6134","diff_url":"https://github.com/obsproject/obs-studio/pull/6134.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/obsproject/obs-studio/pull/6134.patch","merged_at":"2022-07-30T15:27:23Z"},"body":"### Description\r\nThis PR is a stand in replacement of the obs-ffmpeg-mpegts output\r\nwhich currently relies on a pipe to obs-ffmpeg-mux binary.\r\nThis improves srt/rist handling.\r\nAdditionally this fixes several bugs related to auto-reconnect : \r\n- auto-reconnect is partially broken with srt & rist; the UI will display a successful reconnect even though it is not the case\r\nbecause in obs-ffmpeg-mux.c the obs_output_can_begin_data_capture function is not called in the thread doing the reconnect. Fixes: https://github.com/obsproject/obs-studio/issues/6749 \r\n- when non existing urls are used, if auto-reconnect is enabled, obs is locked up.  Fixes: https://github.com/obsproject/obs-studio/issues/5791\r\n\r\n### Motivation and Context\r\nCurrently srt & rist protocols are supported in obs through their implementations\r\nin FFmpeg/avformat.\r\nIt is much preferable to support them natively in obs because this allows for better\r\nlogging and easier debugging. We also don't depend on upstream for bug fixes\r\nor for functionalities.\r\nThis PR achieves this in the following way:\r\n- it creates an obs-ffmpeg-mpegts muxer separate from obs-ffmpeg-mux project;\r\nThe use of obs-ffmpeg-mux allowed for easy support of srt & rist but logging was\r\nan issue.\r\n- it brings the protocol handling in-house by using custom AVIO_Contexts.\r\n\r\nNote that the mpegts muxing is still delegated to avformat library.\r\nThe mpegts spec is quite complex so it doesn't seem reasonable to do the mpegts\r\nmuxing ourselves.\r\nHowever all the protocol handling is now done in obs itself.\r\n\r\nImprovements over the previous srt/rist implementations are the following:\r\n- logging of all protocol stages (opening, writing, closing, failures);\r\n- stats collections (the PR collects stats every 60 seconds; this is not configurable, yet).\r\nThe stats inform on the RTT and the link bandwidth (effective bandwidth from obs to ingest)\r\nfor srt for instance. The figures can be quite useful for optimization of the stream. They could\r\nalso be leveraged for dynamic bitrate.\r\n\r\nFurther improvements are possible but are dependent on whether a better support of these \r\nprotocols is decided upon by the obs dev team. For instance:\r\n- better customize protocol settings (at the plugin level) and create an UI for that.\r\n- add support for multi-track streaming (audio) (this is mostly at UI level).\r\n- add support for opus codec (requires some UI work in obs Settings).\r\n- support rist multi-destinations (rist can stream to up to 10 ingest points).\r\n- support bonding (link aggregation for srt & rist).\r\n\r\n### How Has This Been Tested?\r\nThis was tested on windows 10 & macos 10.15.4 against : \r\n- nimble server,\r\n- wowza server,\r\n- vlc 3 & vlc 4,\r\n- ffplay & ffmpeg.\r\n\r\nWorks fine.\r\n\r\nNOT tested on linux.\r\n\r\nTEST builds here: https://github.com/obsproject/obs-studio/actions/runs/2656507203\r\n\r\n**Important note on deps**\r\nmacos obs-deps require libsrt 1.4.4 and break stats collection with 1.4.1.\r\nThe first commit will be dropped once it's merged into master; it enables the right deps which work with this PR.\r\n\r\n**CI**\r\nCI is currently broken for various reasons on linux, ~~mac & win~~.\r\nOn win: ~~the deps need to ship the import libs of libsrt & librist. This will require an update of obs-deps.~~\r\nOn macOS: ~~the deps do not ship the srt & rist dylibs. This will be fixed by the obs-deps PR mentioned above.~~\r\nOn ubuntu 18.04, the CI script needs to be updated to manually build libsrt & librist. (The ubuntu version is \r\ntoo old to have recent enough packages for srt & rist.)\r\n\r\n### Types of changes\r\n- New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\r\n- Tweak (non-breaking change to improve existing functionality) \r\n- Performance enhancement (non-breaking change which improves efficiency)\r\n- Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\r\n\r\n### Checklist:\r\n- [x] My code has been run through [clang-format](https://github.com/obsproject/obs-studio/blob/master/.clang-format).\r\n- [x] I have read the [**contributing** document](https://github.com/obsproject/obs-studio/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.rst).\r\n- [x] My code is not on the master branch.\r\n- [x] The code has been tested.\r\n- [x] All commit messages are properly formatted and commits squashed where appropriate.\r\n- [x] I have included updates to all appropriate documentation.\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/obsproject/obs-studio/issues/6134/reactions","total_count":9,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":3,"rocket":4,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/obsproject/obs-studio/issues/6134/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":7007169207,